      <div class="case-content">
        <section id="summary">
          <h2>1. Partition model &amp; offline continuity</h2>
          <p>
            Multi-station commercial venues (POS registers, floor tablets, kitchen displays, and field couriers) cannot halt sales during ISP outages — nor can they allow reconnecting nodes to silently overwrite inventory or double-charge customers.
          </p>
          <p>
            Meson layers three complementary resilience mechanisms: <strong>encrypted Rust LAN P2P sync</strong> (clean-room open-sourced in <code>M4QSZ/lan-delta-sync</code>), <strong>transactional Isar WAL idempotency</strong> (<code>meson_db</code>), and an <strong>opportunistic courier mesh relay</strong> in <code>apps/meson_delivery</code> turning delivery smartphones into store-and-forward data mules.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="hlc">
          <h2>2. Hybrid Logical Clocks (HLC) &amp; CRDT convergence</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Causal ordering without perfect clocks (<code>clock.rs</code>, <code>hlc_engine.rs</code>):</strong> <code>HybridLogicalClock</code> pairs physical wall time with a monotonic logical counter and deterministic node ID, guaranteeing <code>e₁ → e₂ ⇒ hlc(e₁) &lt; hlc(e₂)</code> even under skewed terminal clocks.</li>
            <li><strong>Tombstone LWW-CRDT map (<code>crdt.rs</code>):</strong> <code>LwwRegister</code> ensures strong eventual consistency (<code>CvRDT</code>) regardless of packet reordering or duplicate delivery, using bounded tombstones to prevent deleted record resurrection.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="aead">
          <h2>3. Anti-replay AEAD framing &amp; bounded outbox</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Authenticated LAN wire framing (<code>wire.rs</code>):</strong> every <code>DeltaMessage</code> travels inside an <code>EncryptedPacket</code> protected by <code>ChaCha20-Poly1305</code> (and <code>AES-256-GCM</code> + Argon2 on the internal bus) with a sliding-window <code>NonceManager</code> rejecting replayed frames.</li>
            <li><strong>Coalescing bounded outbox (<code>outbox.rs</code> &amp; <code>dart-offline-outbox</code>):</strong> repeated writes to the same entity coalesce locally with jittered exponential backoff, partial batch ACKs, and deterministic dead-letter quarantine.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="wal">
          <h2>4. Local Isar WAL &amp; idempotent execution</h2>
          <p>
            In <code>packages/meson_db/lib/src/adapters/isar_idempotency_adapter.dart</code>, <code>IsarIdempotencyAdapter</code> commits an immutable <code>LocalExecutedTransaction</code> inside atomic <code>isar.writeTxn</code> blocks before enqueuing remote sync. Its <code>hasExecuted</code> / <code>shouldExecute</code> / <code>recordExecution</code> guards guarantee zero duplicate charges or inventory deductions across flaky reconnects.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="mesh">
          <h2>5. Opportunistic courier mesh relay (DTN)</h2>
          <p>
            When a venue loses ISP access while retaining local Wi-Fi, <code>apps/meson_delivery</code> executes a Delay-Tolerant Network relay:
          </p>
          <ol>
            <li><strong>Local discovery (<code>NetworkScannerService</code>):</strong> courier smartphones discover isolated POS hosts over local Wi-Fi via mDNS and IP probing during order pickup.</li>
            <li><strong>Blind encrypted harvesting (<code>MeshRelayService</code>):</strong> pulls encrypted offline transaction batches from <code>/api/relay/sync</code> tagged with carrier metadata (<code>relay_user_id</code>), without granting the courier decryption keys.</li>
            <li><strong>Deferred cloud upload:</strong> once cellular connectivity returns in transit, batches upload to Supabase (<code>mesh_relay_payloads</code>) for idempotent server reconciliation.</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section id="validity">
          <h2>6. CI verification &amp; physical limits</h2>
